                <pb facs="0466" n="294" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp01v01/pg294"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 832.85/37</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Morgan</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-06-03T12:00:00-03:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 3, 1917, noon</hi></date>. <lb/> [<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Received June 4, 1 a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>President of Brazil yesterday issued a decree placing all German merchant vessels
                    anchored in Brazilian ports under the Brazilian flag and directing that they be
                    prepared for sea as soon as possible. The vessels in Rio de Janeiro harbor have
                    already been appropriated, and others under control of Lloyd Brasileiro Company
                    which is under the direction of Ministry of Finance. Appropriation and transfer
                    of flag effected without opposition. Appropriation of vessels in other ports
                    under way.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Morgan</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
